    "updated_at": "2025-02-12T22:22:45Z",
    "body": "There's a trick required here which you can find in the test case for using `pipeThrough()` with a SerialPort's readable stream: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/web_tests/wpt_internal/serial/serialPort_readable_chain.https.any.js\n\nThrough a long chain of transform streams it takes the invocation of a few microtasks for the `SerialPort` to observe that `readable` has been closed. The trick is to use the `Promise` returned by `pipeTo()` to observe when the closure has reached that point, at which point it is safe to call `serialPort.close()`.\n\nJust to be sure it works with an `AbortSignal` I've created a patch to add another test case for that scenario: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/6259266",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
